  "body": "On multiple occasions it is necessary to change a parameter of the current URL and reload the page. For example to change the language or the number of results per page. To do this, a &lt;select&gt; element is usually used with the different options and through Javascript the selection change is detected, the parameter changed and the page reloaded. This is something very used, very useful and very simple that the browser could do without using Javascript. It would only be necessary to indicate in the &lt;select&gt; element that its function is to change a parameter of the URL.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n  ```\r\n<select url-parameter=\"lang\"/>\r\n      <option>en</option>\r\n      <option>es</option>\r\n\r\n  URL = https://demo.nexttypes.com/?lang=en\r\n```",
